keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - technological protectionism
  - compute sovereignty
  - semiconductors export controls
  - European Union strategic autonomy
abstract: >
  Integrated geostrategic and economic study of US AI protectionism under
  the Trump 2.0 administration, crossing energy, semiconductors, compute
  and regulation. Construction of the Compute-Adjusted Competitiveness
  Index (CACI) quantifying a structural US/EU competitive advantage of
  7 to 12 to 1 over the 2026-2030 period. Multilingual support (EN/FR/PT).
